   "text": "# Why Compressed Data Trades CPU for Storage Traffic\n\n## The core mechanism\n\nCompression works by replacing redundant patterns with shorter representations. That transformation is not free:\n\n- **Decompression cost:** Every read must run the inverse transform (e.g., Huffman decoding, LZ77 back-references, entropy decoding) before the data is usable. This is pure added CPU work on the read path.\n- **Compression cost:** Every write must analyze the data and encode it, which is often *more* expensive than decompression (searching for matches, building dictionaries, entropy coding).\n- **Reduced bytes moved:**",
